  "historic_survey": {
    "survey": "Duboce Triangle Historic Context Statement (2022)",
    "source": "duboce-triangle-context-statement",
    "note": "Named with its twin at 736–740 as a good example of the larger flats and apartment buildings that went up in Duboce Triangle between 1893 and 1905, whose box-like massing and near-identical facades gave the northeast of the neighborhood a denser, more urban look. Christopher VerPlanck's context statement of 2022 surveyed 552 properties in Duboce Triangle for the Duboce Triangle Neighborhood Association."
